        <headline>Flood Watch issued September 24 at 3:45PM HST until September 26 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI</headline>
        <description>Intensifying Tropical Storm Nolo is expected to bring heavy flooding
rain to the eastern end of the state over the next few days. The
exact track of the dangerous tropical cyclone remains somewhat
uncertain, but significant heavy rain is likely over windward and
southeast Big Island.

* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be
possible.

* WHERE...Big Island, Maui, Lanai, Molokai, and Kahoolawe.

* WHEN...Through Saturday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of
streams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along
with property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.
Landslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- Deep moisture on the north side of Nolo will bring heavy showers
later  tonight over Big Island and spread to Maui. Windward and
southeast Big Island and windward Maui are the most likely to
experience heavy rain due to the slow moving tropical cyclone,
with considerable flooding possible over portions of Big Island
Friday and Saturday. Other islands in Maui County are at risk as
well.
</description>
        <instruction>You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action
should Flash Flood Warnings be issued.</instruction>
